          "explanation": "We the Living is set in Petrograd in the early 1920s -- exactly where and when Rand lived as a teenager and university student. Her family's pharmacy was confiscated after 1917, and she experienced the class sorting, shortages, and purges that fill the novel. Hollywood came later and shaped her career, not this book's setting; she grew up in St. Petersburg/Petrograd, not Moscow.",
