          "explanation": "In her 1959 foreword, Rand said she edited clumsy phrasing from her early English and tightened sentences, but left the plot, characters, and ideas intact. Some scholars dispute part of this, arguing that softening a few of Kira's Nietzschean lines shifted the book's philosophy slightly toward her later views. That debate is real, but no one claims she changed the ending, added Objectivist chapters, or cut major characters.",
