          "explanation": "Rand's point is that the evil lies in the system itself, not in who runs it. By making Andrei sincere, brave, and incorruptible -- and still destroyed once he sees clearly -- she blocks the reading that better communists would fix things. That makes the second option the opposite of her intent. Critics reply that killing him off also spares her from answering a surviving believer.",
