          "explanation": "Rand lived through Petrograd in the early 1920s, and the novel's texture -- the NEP, rations, communal housing, class-based purges -- reflects real conditions. Critics fault it for compressing events and for drawing most communists, such as Syerov and Sonia, as hypocrites with little genuine idealism; Andrei is the notable exception. So it is neither invented nor neutral, and its weakness lies in motives, not living conditions.",
